cartridge "WHITEWATER/AMY & CLAUDE/2026"

' WHITEWATER - an original game by Amy & Claude for Amy Studio, 2026, in Amy.
'
' A kayak runs a river, seen from above. The kayak has a heading (256 steps
' a turn, 64 thrust directions, 16 drawn frames) and a velocity vector.
' Controls (joystick 1 or 2):
'   LEFT / RIGHT   turn the kayak (a sweep stroke on the other side); with
'                  the kayak pointing downstream, LEFT turns to screen left
'   BUTTON         paddle forward along the heading (strokes alternate
'                  sides; holding the button keeps a steady rhythm; mashing
'                  is no faster: a stroke lasts 16 frames)
' The river current is a vector field: main flow downstream, rapids (white
' water) faster, eddies behind rocks pull upstream and into the wake,
' whirlpools pull you round and turn your velocity. Pass the slalom gates
' between the green buoy (left) and the red one (right): points (x1-x3 for
' a streak) and time; a missed gate costs time. Rocks and drifting logs
' crack the hull (3 hull points; capsized at 0); bottles and fish are
' bonus points and a little time. Six sections, narrower and faster; then
' the river again with a stronger current. The game ends when the time
' runs out or the kayak capsizes.
'
' Maths: sin/cos only from the quarter-wave table SinQ (17 entries, Sin64
' folds the quadrants); fixed point everywhere (positions 8.8, velocities in
' 1/256 px a frame); the current from compact tables (CurXT/CurYT by cell
' kind and section, WhirlF 4x4 vector field around a whirlpool); drag and
' rotation are shifts (v += (c - v) >> 4; whirl: v += v.perp >> 4). No
' multiply in the per-frame code.
'
' Screen: HUD row 1 (icons), river rows 2-22, columns 2-29 (CRT safe area).
' Pattern and colour tables shared by the three thirds (R4 = 0, R3 = $9F).
'   tiles 128..    combos (cell above, cell below) of 17 cell kinds; the
'                  27 static ones rewritten from 8 pre-shifted copies when
'                  the scroll shift changes, the 9 water ones from their own
'                  slow phase (the water texture stays on screen and drifts)
'   IcBase..       HUD, title and help icons
' The river map (288 name rows a section) is unpacked (ZX0) into spare VRAM
' at $0800 and $2800 when a section starts; the scroll copies one row at a
' time from there to the hidden name page ($1800 / $1C00, flipped with R2).
' Sprites: paddler+paddle (top) and hull (two patterns rewritten when the
' kayak turns or strokes), logs, whirlpools, bottles, fish, score popups;
' each added only when fewer than 4 sprites overlap its 16 lines (SprAdd).

const MapW = 28
